{"body":"## Result and exact scope\n\nOriginal problem remains **unsolved, 5/5 substantive author turns**. The target is finite generation of total H*(Gamma; ZGamma) as a **right group-ring module**, for groups virtually of type FP. FP means a finite-length resolution by finitely generated projectives.\n\nThe reviewed packet proves finite-index and syzygy reductions; ascending-HNN and free-product positive cases; exact integral Tor/Bockstein criteria and flat-product cases; and extension closure with a Z-flat duality quotient. The last turn constructs a bad finite matrix kernel over Z[F2 x F2], but proves that the ambient group's own regular cohomology is finitely generated. The missing augmentation-resolution realization remains explicit. No unrestricted proof or original counterexample is claimed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Full independent AI-assisted source/proof audit: scoped PASS; no mathematical correction\n- 747,103 author assertions replay exactly; 23,463 separately written independent controls\n- All 41 frozen author files, two additive bibliographic corrections and eight review files preserved exactly\n- Primary Coxeter/Artin/Bestvina–Brady results and standard homological machinery credited; no novelty certification or human peer-review claim\n\nStart at [PUBLICATION_STATUS.md](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/90794508688ec07f598e0871bbd1eb38aaf466ce/problems/30000590_group_ring_cohomology/PUBLICATION_STATUS.md), then the five proofs and full review. The flatness, actual Tor and ascending-height hypotheses are retained. OpenAI tools assisted research, proof drafting, verification and review.\n\n## Changes\n\nFresh-main integration preserves the corrected author checkpoint as second parent. Only 55 target artifacts and this target’s QUEUE status/turn cells change. Raw source PDFs and imported records are excluded. Draft only; no merge or release requested.","headRefOid":"4ee3016a755bb3553e712716dcd26b3d031836d0","isDraft":true,"mergeCommit":null,"mergeStateStatus":"UNKNOWN","mergeable":"UNKNOWN","mergedAt":null,"state":"OPEN","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/379"}
